{"skill":{"slug":"nexo-brain","displayName":"NEXO Desktop Runtime"},"version":{"version":"7.38.7","createdAt":1782628196486,"changelog":"Release v7.38.7 - NEXO Desktop runtime core","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3453,"sha256":"159b907290f6896738d2bc073d1beffccc25249d676ef6688028a7b819363635","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1922,"sha256":"8ad8eadc91be0fe444b8d5ac7225e2058f786db55903faf60f899c1ce9d22697","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789432155815,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"cb22c75918c9d1fdf7e82fdfdda128f9bb40817944176eae2db338ee9d74c999","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/cb22c75918c9d1fdf7e82fdfdda128f9bb40817944176eae2db338ee9d74c999","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1782628308197},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":9,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789432155815},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This is a coherent NEXO Desktop runtime installer, but it asks users to execute an unpinned npm package that can install a persistent local MCP runtime.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The runtime is scoped to local storage under `~/.nexo/` and an OpenClaw MCP config entry, which is proportionate for a local memory service, but support/improvement ticket data flow is only briefly described as anonymized.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The install metadata names the npm package `nexo-brain` without an exact version, and the manual setup uses bare `npx nexo-brain`; despite the skill version being 7.38.7, the executable package resolved at install time can change after review.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill describes broad runtime behavior such as heartbeat on every interaction, semantic retrieval across memories, and session continuity; this is purpose-aligned but gives the runtime ongoing visibility into agent context.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The user is instructed to register `~/.nexo/server.py` as a Python MCP server and restart the gateway, creating cross-session execution; this is disclosed and user-directed, but it compounds the unpinned installer risk.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, local memory/runtime capabilities, watchdog, Deep Sleep, and MCP tools fit together as a desktop runtime core, and those capabilities are mostly disclosed in the skill text.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust the `nexo-brain` npm package and publisher. Prefer an exact reviewed version, verify what creates `~/.nexo/server.py`, and be aware that the runtime maintains local memory and can run through the OpenClaw gateway across sessions.","findings":"[RP1] unexpected: Confirmed in `SKILL.md`: the npm-based runtime install is purpose-aligned, but the unpinned `npx nexo-brain` command is not necessary for that purpose and leaves the reviewed skill dependent on whatever package version is current at install time.\n[T08] unexpected: Confirmed in `SKILL.md`: the package name is unversioned in install metadata and manual setup. This supports a Review verdict for supply-chain and persistent MCP execution risk, but the artifact does not show deception, exfiltration, destructive behavior, or privilege escalation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789432155815}}}}}